<Prose title="How We Score Backup Power Gear: The AMB Score Method" description="How the AMB Score works: spec-sheet analysis, load maths, safety features and owner-reported reliability, weighted by category. What we claim and what we don't." h1="How We Score: The AMB Score" path="/how-we-test/" intro="Every product we cover gets an AMB Score out of 100. Here is exactly what goes into it.">
  <h2>What the Score Is Built On</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>The spec sheet, read properly.</strong> We read past the headline numbers to the conditions behind them: running vs starting (peak) watts, rated vs surge output on an inverter, usable vs nominal watt-hours, decibels at what load and distance, LiFePO4 vs NMC cycle ratings.</li>
    <li><strong>Load maths.</strong> We convert specs into what they mean in an outage: which appliances a generator can start together, how many hours a power station runs a fridge or CPAP, how much fuel a weekend outage burns. Our <a href="/tools/generator-wattage-calculator/">wattage</a> and <a href="/tools/power-station-runtime-calculator/">runtime</a> calculators use the same formulas.</li>
    <li><strong>Safety features.</strong> CO shutoff (Honda CO-MINDER, Champion CO Shield, Generac COsense and similar), GFCI outlets, transfer-switch readiness and certifications such as UL and CARB/EPA compliance.</li>
    <li><strong>Owner-reported reliability.</strong> We read owner reviews and forum reports for recurring failures, hard starts, firmware problems and support issues over time.</li>
    <li><strong>Value and fit.</strong> Every product is judged against its class and the buyer it suits, so a small inverter can outrank a bigger, louder open-frame unit for its job.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Category Weightings</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>What we weight most</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Generators</td><td>Running and starting watts, fuel options and run time, noise, CO shutoff, transfer-switch outlets (L14-30 / 14-50), service network</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Inverter generators</td><td>Clean power (THD), noise at load, weight, parallel capability, run time per gallon</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Power stations and home batteries</td><td>Usable capacity, continuous and surge output, LiFePO4 cycle rating, recharge speed (AC and solar), expandability, UPS switchover</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Transfer switches and surge protection</td><td>Code-compliant connection, circuit count and amperage, UL listing, protection ratings</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Outage essentials</td><td>Runtime on a charge, charging options, safety (indoor-rated heat, NOAA alerts), durability</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <h2>What We Don't Claim</h2>
  <p>We do not run a test lab, and we never say "we tested" unless we have. Our guides are built from manufacturer spec sheets and manuals, listings, certifications and owner reports. The AMB Score expresses our editorial ranking within each guide from that research; it is not a bench measurement. When we add hands-on impressions in future, we will say so clearly on the page.</p>
  <h2>Score Bands</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>90–100:</strong> our top pick in its class.</li>
    <li><strong>85–89:</strong> excellent; an easy recommendation for the right buyer.</li>
    <li><strong>78–84:</strong> good with clear trade-offs, or the best fit for a narrower need.</li>
    <li><strong>Below 78:</strong> we'd buy something else.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Prices</h2>
  <p>Generator and power station prices move with sales, stock and storm season, so we don't print them. Every product links to its current price.</p>
  <h2>Updates</h2>
  <p>We review our best lists regularly, and whenever a major model launches or is discontinued. The "Updated" date on each page shows the last substantive revision.</p>
</Prose>
